WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:08.220
Support for Donald Trump's impeachment has
exploded drastically since the start of the

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.910
impeachment inquiry against Donald Trump was
announced last week.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:17.830
Half of those who have an opinion about this
say that the impeachment process should start.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:23.050
It's 43 to 43 with about 13% undecided.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:31.740
This 43% number is up nearly 20% from the
last poll, which had only 36% supporting impeachment.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:35.360
That is now up to 43% that is a 20% increase.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.030
Don't email me and say I'm wrong.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.780
I'm not saying it's a 20 percentage point
increase.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.660
It's a 20% increase.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:49.360
Very importantly, support for impeachment
is up, not just among Democrats.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:54.610
Also among some Republicans and even some
independent support for the impeachment inquiry

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:58.390
has increased and let's dig into it a little
more to get a better understanding.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.260
Uh, there's an argument.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:07.619
The argument is support for impeachment will
go up as more information from the impeachment

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:12.540
inquiry comes out and people realize what
it is Donald Trump is accused of doing.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.009
The poll has data that supports that assertion.

00:01:15.009 --> 00:01:21.740
Shockingly, in this poll, only 34% of Americans
say that they heard some about the Ukraine

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:22.790
fiasco.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:28.760
Another 34% in this poll say they haven't
heard much or anything about the Ukraine fiasco,

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:34.959
so understand that with 68% of respondents
saying they've either heard nothing, not much

00:01:34.959 --> 00:01:41.659
or only some about the Ukraine fiasco, 43%
still support impeachment.

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:47.270
This supports the idea that as people learn
about what has taken place support for impeachment

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.889
will go up even more.

00:01:48.889 --> 00:01:53.009
This poll, by the way, was taken before we
heard from acting director of national intelligence,

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:56.039
Joe Maguire in congressional testimony.

00:01:56.039 --> 00:01:59.670
This was a poll taken before the release of
the recording in which Donald Trump implies

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:04.380
that the whistle blower or the informant to
the whistleblower should be killed.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.240
This 43% support level was before.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:12.989
Lots of the things that we've since learned,
and then we have a newer CBS news poll where

00:02:12.989 --> 00:02:20.790
55% of Americans approve with the impeachment
inquiry an even higher number, meaning 55

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:27.150
minus 36 is 1919 divided by 36 that's more
than a 50% increase, not percentage point,

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:32.470
more than a 50% increase from one before all
of this from before all of this started.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:38.860
Now that all being said, this impeachment
inquiry could still backfire on Democrats.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:44.810
The reference point is look at how bill Clinton's
impeachment backfired on Republicans in the

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.900
1990s that's a fair point of contrast.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:51.370
Although there were some important differences
with the bill Clinton situation.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:55.709
Clinton generally was more likable than Trump,
but that's not my opinion.

00:02:55.709 --> 00:03:01.530
That's the polling bill Clinton didn't interfere
in the impeachment process while Trump already

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.769
is and certainly will continue to do so.

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:05.769
Clinton's impeachment.

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:11.310
In the end, he lied, but he lied, uh, related
